HTML Intro

.standard language for creating and structuring web pages using tags and elements
.defines how content like text, images, and links appear in a browser
.markup language - it annotates text to define how it is structured and displayed in web browsers
.static - doesn't provide interactive features 
    .can be combined with CSS for styling and JS for interactivity


Elements 
.complete structure with tags and content
    <p class='text'>Hello Adagga</p>
.tag - the actual keyword/name enclosed in angle brackets that tells the browser what kind of context to expect 

<html> - root element; contains all the other tags 
<head> - section containing info like the page title 
<body> - section containing the visible content shown in the browser 
